</PolyStyle></Style><name>Brassica</name><description><![CDATA[<p>A cabbage of impeccable lineage, Brassica hails from the noble house of <em>Brassica oleracea</em> (same as the kales, the broccolis, and her adorable little cousins, the Brussels). During a long season in the soil, she dreamed of a life on the road, untethered to just one patch of dirt. While her relatives resigned themselves to slaws and stir-fries, Brassica turned her visions into reality: she pulled up her roots, brushed herself off, and began her quest to be the best-traveled vegetable in the Pacific Northwest.</p>

<p>A longtime beacon of the Seattle geocaching community, she is now the patron cabbage and official mascot of &quot;CABBAGES: Conversations at Ballard Breweries About Geocaching&quot;. She recently discovered the joy of a craft beer on a sunny summer day, and plans to sample Ballard&#39;s finest all season long while befriending as many geocachers as possible. Brassica is equal parts grande dame and field agent: she has strong opinions about LPCs, she will not tolerate a soggy logbook, and she believes deeply that one should&nbsp;<em><strong>leaf no cache behind</strong></em>.&nbsp;🥬</p>
Brassica has traveled 1.67083796083755 miles.]]></description><Folder><Style /><name>Travel Bug Stops (1.67083796083755 mile(s))</name><open>0</open><Placemark><name>GCBN82V</name><Point><coordinates>-122.3777,47.665,100 
